{'symbol': 'WMT', 'date': '2020-05-19 09:30:00', 'title': 'WALMART REPORTS Q1 GAAP EARNINGS OF $1.40 PER SHARE', 'text': "Q1 FY21 GAAP EPS OF $1.40.Q1 ADJUSTED EPS OF $1.18.QUARTERLY TOTAL REVENUE WAS $134.6 BILLION, AN INCREASE OF $10.7 BILLION, OR 8.6%.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.12, REVENUE VIEW $132.79 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.WITHDRAWING FINANCIAL GUIDANCE FOR FISCAL YEAR 2021.EXCLUDING CURRENCY, QUARTERLY TOTAL REVENUE WOULD HAVE INCREASED 9.7% TO REACH $135.9 BILLION.COMPANY INCURS INCREMENTAL COSTS RELATED TO COVID-19 OF NEARLY $900 MILLION IN QUARTER.QUARTERLY WALMART U.S. Q1 COMP SALES GREW 10.0% AND WALMART U.S. ECOMMERCE SALES GREW 74%.SAYS COMPANY'S QUARTERLY NET SALES AND OPERATING RESULTS WERE SIGNIFICANTLY AFFECTED BY OUTBREAK OF COVID-19.SAYS UNPRECEDENTED DEMAND FOR PRODUCTS ACROSS MULTIPLE CATEGORIES LED TO STRONG QUARTERLY TOP-LINE RESULTS.QUARTERLY NET SALES $133.67 BILLION VERSUS $122.95 BILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.SAYS COMPANY WILL DISCONTINUE JET.COM.SAM'S CLUB QUARTERLY COMP SALES INCREASED 12.0%, LED BY IN-CLUB TRANSACTIONS.QUARTERLY WALMART U.S. ECOMMERCE SALES SAW STRONG RESULTS FOR GROCERY PICKUP AND DELIVERY SERVICES, WALMART.COM AND MARKETPLACE.SAYS SHORT-TERM ENVIRONMENT WILL BE CHALLENGING.QUARTERLY WALMART U.S. NET SALES $88,743 MILLION, UP 10.5%.QUARTERLY ADJUSTED EPS EXCLUDES ONLY EFFECTS OF UNREALIZED GAIN OF $0.22, NET OF TAX, ON EQUITY INVESTMENT IN JD.COM.QUARTERLY WALMART INTERNATIONAL NET SALES $29,766 MILLION, UP 3.4%."}{'symbol': 'WMT', 'date': '2020-05-19 09:30:00', 'title': 'WALMART REPORTS Q1 GAAP EARNINGS OF $1.40 PER SHARE', 'text': "Q1 FY21 GAAP EPS OF $1.40.Q1 ADJUSTED EPS OF $1.18.QUARTERLY TOTAL REVENUE WAS $134.6 BILLION, AN INCREASE OF $10.7 BILLION, OR 8.6%.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.12, REVENUE VIEW $132.79 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.WITHDRAWING FINANCIAL GUIDANCE FOR FISCAL YEAR 2021.EXCLUDING CURRENCY, QUARTERLY TOTAL REVENUE WOULD HAVE INCREASED 9.7% TO REACH $135.9 BILLION.COMPANY INCURS INCR